ed with candidate 0. But item 1 keeps only 4 days, so each batch must cover a full cycle with no carryover, and they are more exposed to shortages. Candidate 5's larger orders go over capacity. I estimate about 152 units around day 7 and about 168 around day 15, and the excess is lost after it's paid for. So 5 is clearly worse than 4.\n6. **Candidate 7** orders every 2 days: 14 order days, about 200 more in fees than candidate 0, with moderate volumes.\n7. **Candidate 3** orders almost every day, about 1,370 in daily fees. Its quantities roughly match the forecast with no safety margin, so random swings will cause shortages. It's most likely in the bottom half.\n\nMy estimated ranking is 6 ≈ 0 > 2 > 4 ≈ 1 > 7 > 5 > 3. The probabilities add up to 4, since exactly four candidates are in the top half."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 4653, "cache_read_input_tokens": 2313, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 4653}, "output_tokens": 3, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-28T22:57:40.646Z", "request_id": "req_011CgVTjX5QNeSAQix7k5sJR"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 2, "content_block": {"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01C4DDs6hXDFKvyAH4Y9sH6d", "name": "StructuredOutput", "input": {}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgVTjXJJD7oSQ6L1eDhqg", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01C4DDs6hXDFKvyAH4Y9sH6d", "name": "StructuredOutput", "input": {"p": [0